WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.265 --> 00:00:01.640
CASSIE KOZYRKOV:
This week, we're

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:04.730
talking about BigQuery,
anomaly detection, and data

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:05.720
engineering.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.560
I'm Cassie Kozyrkov, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.710
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:15.500
BigQuery already lets
you analyze petabytes

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.330
of data at lightning speed.

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.550
And it just got even
better with the addition

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:22.280
of a bunch of cool new
features, including

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:25.670
new user-defined functions,
faster reporting capabilities,

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.340
increased concurrency
limits, and new functions

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.080
for encryption and GIS.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.830
The bottom line, helping you get
more out of your data faster.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:37.040
See the article for
tutorials and demo links.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.990
Last year, we
announced BigQuery ML,

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:40.490
bringing supervised
machine learning

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.530
to your multi-petabyte data set.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:45.110
And now, we've
added unsupervised

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:46.880
learning capabilities, too.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.590
In this blog post,
you'll learn how

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:51.170
to train a machine learning
model to catch surprises

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:55.070
in your data, all without having
to write a single line of code

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:56.930
outside of BigQuery SQL.

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:58.610
Check out the full story.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:00.350
And while we're on
the topic of SQL,

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.450
let's talk about
database migration.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.000
If you're keen to migrate
your MySQL database to Cloud

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.910
SQL, our fully-managed
database service designed

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:10.340
to take care of that
heavy lifting for you,

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:13.160
you might want to check out
this new hands-on tutorial

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:16.790
for setting up your
automated migration workflow.

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:18.710
For the data
engineers among you,

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:21.800
we're excited to announce a
professional Data Engineer

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:26.450
Certification exam to put that
spotlight on your expertise.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:29.120
Go earn your certificate
today and get noticed faster

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:30.517
for high-demand roles.

00:01:30.517 --> 00:01:32.600
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.550
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:37.170
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:39.030
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:42.040
We'll see you in the cloud.

